# Docker image safety

Run as a non-root user when the project's existing images already do. Do not
switch a root image to non-root (or the reverse) unless that is the task.

Pin tags or digests when surrounding Dockerfiles already pin. Do not float
`latest` in a file that previously pinned.

Never put secrets in `ENV` or `ARG` that land in image layers. Use runtime
secret mounts the repo already uses.

Do not run `docker build --network=host` without asking the user.
